The full contraction identity expands products of two epsilons into Kronecker deltas:
$ epsilon_(i j k) epsilon_(p q r) = delta_(i p) delta_(j q) delta_(k r) + delta_(i q) delta_(j r) delta_(k p) + delta_(i r) delta_(j p) delta_(k q) - delta_(i p) delta_(j r) delta_(k q) - delta_(i q) delta_(j p) delta_(k r) - delta_(i r) delta_(j q) delta_(k p). $
Contracting indices gives the workhorse forms
$ epsilon_(i j k) epsilon_(p q k) = delta_(i p) delta_(j q) - delta_(i q) delta_(j p), quad epsilon_(i j k) epsilon_(p j k) = 2 delta_(i p), quad epsilon_(i j k) epsilon_(i j k) = 6. $
